# Line endings are LF in the repository AND in every working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. `apps/web/index.html` carries an inline script that the
# Content-Security-Policy admits by SHA-256 hash, and a hash covers exact bytes — so a
# working tree checked out with CRLF hashes differently from the one the policy was written
# against, and a build made from it ships a policy that refuses its own script. The failure
# is silent in the browser and invisible in CI, because CI runs on Linux and gets LF.
#
# Git already stored LF; only Windows working trees were converted on checkout. Setting this
# therefore changes no file content, only what lands on disk.
#
# It also stops a second, quieter problem: transform scripts anchored on "\n" match nothing
# in a CRLF file and exit zero, which cost real time during the M4 design pass.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never converted or diffed as text.
*.woff2 binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
